What is opportunity cost? Explain with the help of a numerical example.
Opportunity cost for a commodity is the amount of other commodity that has been
foregone in order to produce additional unit of the first. e.g. if a person A is working in
a bank and gets a job offer of a journalist. A as a bank executive, gets 40,000 and as
journalist would get ₹45,000 In this case, the opportunity cost of being a journalist is
₹40,000, which is the second best opportunity.
