Why is production possibility curve called opportunity cost curve?
Production possibility curve is also called opportunity cost curve because slope of the
curve at each and every point measures opportunity cost of one commodity in term of
alternative commodity given up. The rate of this sacrifice is called the marginal
opportunity cost of the expanding good.
